    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/01/mizuno-neo-zen-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length ENERZY NXT delivers a very soft, highly protective ride in both heel and forefoot, with heavy compression that makes the 40/34 mm stack and 6 mm drop feel lower.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole is notably bouncy, but turnover is moderate rather than snappy; it can handle small pace pickups yet feels best for easy/long runs, not fast efforts.",
        "Stability: Platform stiffness is moderate with minimal forefoot flex, but rearfoot structure is flexible (no traditional heel counter); lockdown relies on knit upper overlays/circular heel panels and was generally secure with limited foot translation.",
        "Durability: Reported as above average, with extensive outsole coverage showing virtually no wear after ~30 miles and midsole feel holding up well, suggesting strong material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/01/mizuno-neo-zen-multi-tester-review-art.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Max-cushion setup (39.5 mm heel / 33.5 mm forefoot) is notably soft and plush with strong impact protection, with heel feel described as especially soft/bouncy; some testers felt it could verge on mushy.",
        "Responsiveness: The nitrogen/supercritical TPU foam is consistently described as energetic and bouncy, giving strong perceived energy return and a fun, snappy-enough ride for a plateless trainer.",
        "Stability: Broad platform and secure upper/lockdown help lateral stability, but rearfoot support is a weakness because heel counter/collar structure is minimal; this may be less stable for pronation control, slower paces, and heel-strike landings.",
        "Durability: This excerpt does not provide meaningful outsole wear or long-term material longevity data, so durability is not yet clearly established."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/mizuno-neo-zen-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: High-stack geometry (40 mm heel / 34 mm forefoot, 6 mm drop) is described as soft and comfortable, with strong underfoot protection for daily training at any distance.",
        "Responsiveness: The Enerzy NXT midsole is characterized as super bouncy, indicating strong energy return and a lively ride even without a plate.",
        "Stability: Despite the soft ride, the shoe is noted as surprisingly stable, with a wide base, secure lockdown, and no reported heel slippage supporting lateral control.",
        "Durability: The provided excerpt gives no direct long-term outsole wear or upper/longevity results, so durability remains unconfirmed from this text alone."
      ]
